"text":"இதழ்","lemma":"itaḻ","gloss":"petal"}],"gloss":"petal"},{"surface":"அழிந்து","parts":[{"text":"அழி","lemma":"aḻi","gloss":"ruin"},{"text":"ந்து","lemma":"ntu","gloss":"past adverbial participle suffix"}],"gloss":"having ruined"},{"surface":"ஊறும்","parts":[{"text":"ஊறு","lemma":"ūṟu","gloss":"ooze/flow"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"relative participle suffix"}],"gloss":"flowing"},{"surface":"கண்","parts":[{"text":"கண்","lemma":"kaṇ","gloss":"eye"}],"gloss":"eye"},{"surface":"பனி","parts":[{"text":"பனி","lemma":"pani","gloss":"tear/dew"}],"gloss":"tear"},{"surface":"மதர்","parts":[{"text":"மதர்","lemma":"matar","gloss":"luxuriant/beautiful"}],"gloss":"beautiful"},{"surface":"எழில்","parts":[{"text":"எழில்","lemma":"eḻil","gloss":"grace/beauty"}],"gloss":"grace"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பூணக","parts":[{"text":"பூண்","lemma":"pūṇ","gloss":"ornament"},{"text":"அக","lemma":"aka","gloss":"inside/place"}],"gloss":"chest where ornaments lie"},{"surface":"வன","parts":[{"text":"வன","lemma":"வன","gloss":"beautiful"}],"gloss":"beautiful","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"முலை","parts":[{"text":"முலை","lemma":"mulai","gloss":"breast"}],"gloss":"breast"},{"surface":"நனைத்தலும்","parts":[{"text":"நனைத்தல்","lemma":"naṉaittal","gloss":"wetting"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"even/and"}],"gloss":"even wetting"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"காணார்","parts":[{"text":"காண்","lemma":"kāṇ","gloss":"see"},{"text":"ஆர்","lemma":"ār","gloss":"negative third person plural suffix"}],"gloss":"will they not see?"},{"surface":"கொல்லோ","parts":[{"text":"கொல்","lemma":"kol","gloss":"particle of doubt"},{"text":"ஓ","lemma":"ō","gloss":"clitic"}],"gloss":"indeed?"},{"surface":"மாண்","parts":[{"text":"மாண்","lemma":"māṇ","gloss":"excellent"}],"gloss":"excellent"},{"surface":"இழை","parts":[{"text":"இழை","lemma":"iḻai","gloss":"jeweled ornaments"}],"gloss":"jeweled ornaments"},{"surface":"நமரே","parts":[{"text":"நமர்","lemma":"namar","gloss":"our lover"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"our lover"}]}],"literal":"By themselves they will go, in the path of the forest / where pasture-seeking elephants' tusks-between left-behind / small-blossomed jasmine branch spreading / petals ruined, oozing eye-tears, beautiful, graceful / ornament-bearing beautiful breasts wetting / will he not see indeed, our man of excellent jewels?","translation":"Our lover, who left us, will surely travel by himself along the forest paths. There, the small-blossomed jasmine branches, caught and left behind between the tusks of pasture-seeking elephants, scatter their ruined petals. Will he not see how my eyes, like those ruined blossoms, overflow with tears that wet my beautiful breasts adorned with fine jewels?","modern":"மேய்ச்சலைத் தேடிச் செல்லும் யானைகளின் தந்தங்களுக்கு இடையே சிக்கித் தப்பிய சிறிய பூக்களைக் கொண்ட முல்லைக் கொடியிலிருந்து உதிர்ந்து, இதழ்கள் சிதைந்து பரவியிருக்கும் முல்லைப் பூக்களைப் போல, என் கண்களிலிருந்து வழியும் கண்ணீர் என் அழகிய மார்பகங்களை நனைப்பதை, நம் தலைவர் அந்தப் பாலைவனக் காட்டு வழியில் செல்லும்போது காணமாட்டாரோ?","explanation":"The friend (தோழி) speaks to the heroine (தலைவி) or to herself in the heroine's presence, expressing deep concern about the hero's journey through the arid desert (pālai). The poem uses a vivid image of a jasmine branch caught between the tusks of an elephant searching for pasture. As the elephant moves, the delicate jasmine blossoms are crushed and scattered. This is compared to the heroine's eyes, which are ruined by weeping, shedding tears that wet her beautiful breasts. The comparison of the crushed jasmine petals to the tear-filled eyes of the grieving heroine highlights the pain of separation. The key words are 'முல்லை' (jasmine), 'யானைக் கோடு' (elephant's tusk), 'கண்பனி' (tears), and 'காணார் கொல்லோ' (will he not see?).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}